{
  "title": "把海上的人帶回家",
  "title_en": "Bringing Them Home",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 5,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-bringing-them-home",
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 22,
  "setting": "留著一盞燈的漁港",
  "subtitle": "一則海港守護故事",
  "subtitle_en": "A Harbour Story of Guardianship",
  "lead": "還有人在海上，誰替他們留著回來的位置？她把華服拆成紅色的屏，有人守燈，有人等在碼頭，有人把熱湯放上桌。守護，是把接應的工作一起做完。",
  "lead_en": "Who keeps a place ready for those still at sea? She turns her finery into red screens. Others tend the lamps, wait by the quay, and put soup on the table. Protection becomes the work they share.",
  "statement": "還有人在海上，誰替他們留著回來的位置？她把華服拆成紅色的屏，有人守燈，有人等在碼頭，有人把熱湯放上桌。守護，是把接應的工作一起做完。\n\n紅衣與燈火，呼應媽祖海洋守護敘事中的意象。《天妃顯聖錄》寫朱衣現於桅竿，郁永河〈海上紀略〉記下桅端的光。故事把這些意象帶回岸上：一位海上守護女神與港邊的人一起立起紅屏，留燈，也留一碗熱湯。",
  "statement_en": "Who keeps a place ready for those still at sea? She turns her finery into red screens. Others tend the lamps, wait by the quay, and put soup on the table. Protection becomes the work they share.\n\nRed cloth and lamplight echo images in Mazu's maritime guardianship stories. The Tianfei Xiansheng Lu describes a red-robed figure at a ship's mast; Yu Yonghe's Haishang Jilüe records light at the masthead. Here, these images come ashore: a sea guardian goddess works with the harbour's people to raise red screens, keep lamps ready, and set out a bowl of hot soup.",
  "afterword": "",
  "afterword_en": "",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "紅衣與燈火，呼應媽祖海洋守護敘事中的意象。《天妃顯聖錄》寫朱衣現於桅竿，郁永河〈海上紀略〉記下桅端的光。故事把這些意象帶回岸上：一位海上守護女神與港邊的人一起立起紅屏，留燈，也留一碗熱湯。",
  "story_en": "Red cloth and lamplight echo images in Mazu's maritime guardianship stories. The Tianfei Xiansheng Lu describes a red-robed figure at a ship's mast; Yu Yonghe's Haishang Jilüe records light at the masthead. Here, these images come ashore: a sea guardian goddess works with the harbour's people to raise red screens, keep lamps ready, and set out a bowl of hot soup.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：《天妃顯聖錄》〈朱衣著靈〉（https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/54777/pg54777-images.html）；郁永河《裨海紀遊》〈海上紀略〉（https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/裨海紀遊/海上紀略）",
  "sources_en": "Story references: 《天妃顯聖錄》〈朱衣著靈〉 (https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/54777/pg54777-images.html); 郁永河《裨海紀遊》〈海上紀略〉 (https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/裨海紀遊/海上紀略)",
  "credit": "史旺基 Swanky 企劃、視覺統籌、選片與審定。",
  "credit_en": "Concept, visual direction, image selection and editorial oversight by Swanky.",
